{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And also his blood — behold, it is required.</b> The word ״גַּם״ (also) appears to call for explanation, for the brothers thought that Joseph was liable to the death penalty according to law, since evil speech kills three parties, and Joseph brought an evil report about them — it is as though he had killed them. Moreover, he came to spy on them when he came to Dothan; therefore they sought legal stratagems according to the Torah to put him to death before he could draw near to them and kill them, for ״the one who comes to kill you — rise early to kill him first״ (Sanhedrin 72a). If so, from the side of their seeking to kill him they bore no guilt according to their reasoning. But the principal guilt is the measure of cruelty that was in them, that they did not listen when he pleaded with them, as they themselves said: ״but we are guilty concerning our brother, in that we saw the distress of his soul when he pleaded with us and we did not listen; therefore has this trouble come upon us״ (Genesis 42:21). And they did not mention that they had sought to kill him, because they thought that from the side of seeking to kill him, or of selling him, or of casting him into the pit, there was no guilt upon them. And Reuben answered them: ״Did I not speak to you, saying, Do not sin against the child?״ (Genesis 42:22) — since he is like a child and is not yet subject to punishment in the heavenly court, if so there is no death-penalty due to him. And if so, there are two transgressions in your hands: for the Holy One, blessed be He, requires of you the measure of cruelty, for therefore this ruler does not hear our supplication — for we all speak entreaties and he answers with harshness. And in addition to this, ״also his blood — behold, it is required״: for the ruler said ״and your words will be verified and you shall not die״ (Genesis 42:20) — hear from this that if our brother does not come, we are sons of death. And who knows whether our younger brother will reach him at such a time, for perhaps some accident may occur that he will not be able to come to him, and then we are condemned to death. And though in truth we are innocent of his blood, this is only because ״also his blood — behold, it is required,״ in addition to the requiring of the measure of cruelty from our hands."], :book :genesis, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:33:14.390174234Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}